## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-account data flows with privacy and governance, real-time ML inference, and cost controls in an enterprise multi-tenant environment.

## Key Concepts
- Event-driven architecture: S3 Events → Lambda → SageMaker → DynamoDB
- Data privacy: PII masking via pattern matching, KMS encryption at rest/transit
- Data governance: Glue Data Catalog for lineage and schema registry
- Cross-account access: RAM shared resources with service control policies
- Operational excellence: Idempotent writes (deduplication via record keys), DLQ for failures, exponential backoff

## Code Example
```javascript
export const handler = async (event) => {
  const { bucket, key } = event.Records[0].s3.object;
  const data = await s3.getObject({ Bucket: bucket, Key: key }).promise();

  const masked = maskPII(data);
  const { predictions } = await sageMaker.invokeEndpoint({
    EndpointName: process.env.ENDPOINT_NAME,
    ContentType: 'application/json',
    Body: JSON.stringify(masked)
  }).promise();

  const item = { id: uuid(), timestamp: Date.now(), scores: predictions, recordKey: key };
  await dynamo.put({ TableName: process.env.TABLE_NAME, Item: item, ConditionExpression: 'attribute_not_exists(id)' }).promise();

  await glue.updateTable({ DatabaseName: 'lineage', TableInput: tableInput });
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test end-to-end privacy controls?
- How to handle throttling on SageMaker endpoints at scale?
- What cost optimization strategies apply to high-volume inference?

## Why This Question Is Asked

This question tests end-to-end design skills for complex data workflows involving sensitive data, combining multiple AWS AI services, data protection mechanisms, and cost controls.

## Key Concepts

- Textract AnalyzeDocument for structured data extraction from forms and tables
- Comprehend for document classification and PII entity detection
- Layout-preserving redaction techniques
- Event-driven orchestration using Step Functions
- Dual-output storage in S3 with DynamoDB indexing
- IAM least privilege principles, KMS encryption, dead-letter queues, retry logic, and cost controls

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Comment": "State machine outline",
  "StartAt": "Ingest",
  "States": {
    "Ingest": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "S3TriggerLambda"
      },
      "Next": "TextractAnalysis"
    },
    "TextractAnalysis": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::aws-sdk:textract/analyzeDocument",
      "Parameters": {
        "Document": {
          "S3Object": {
            "Bucket.$": "$.bucket",
            "Name.$": "$.key"
          }
        },
        "FeatureTypes": ["FORMS", "TABLES"]
      },
      "Next": "ComprehendClassification"
    },
    "ComprehendClassification": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::aws-sdk:comprehend:classifyDocument",
      "Parameters": {
        "EndpointArn": "arn:aws:comprehend:region:account:endpoint/document-classifier",
        "Text": "$($.extractedText)"
      },
      "Next": "RedactPII"
    },
    "RedactPII": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "RedactionLambda"
      },
      "Next": "StoreArtifacts"
    },
    "StoreArtifacts": {
      "Type": "Parallel",
      "Branches": [
        {
          "StartAt": "StoreOriginal",
          "States": {
            "StoreOriginal": {
              "Type": "Pass",
              "End": true
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "StartAt": "StoreRedacted",
          "States": {
            "StoreRedacted": {
              "Type": "Pass",
              "End": true
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "Next": "UpdateDynamoDB"
    },
    "UpdateDynamoDB": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::dynamodb:putItem",
      "Parameters": {
        "TableName": "contracts-index",
        "Item": {
          "contractId": {"S": "$($.contractId)"},
          "origKey": {"S": "$($.origKey)"},
          "redactedKey": {"S": "$($.redactedKey)"},
